# ATMOS placement (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (p), RULED 2026-10-18; Dave asked whether the screen belongs on a
# Reference only).  Measured: the element TYPE does not matter -- the RAY-grid screen is sampled by grid index and
# tilts the rays along xGrid / yGrid, so it is right wherever the ray grid at the element is still the source grid
# (index i along +xGrid, j along +yGrid, the beam along zGrid) and wrong where a fold, image rotation or inversion
# has intervened.  The Cassegrain's SECONDARY (a Reflector in the converging beam) is accepted and consistent
# (spot = 0.965 EFL x grad W); on the periscope fixture tst_atmos_fold.in the plane BETWEEN the folds (beam along
# +x, xGrid along the beam: pre-fix the x tilt went longitudinal, spot x 1e-8 vs 7e-5) is REFUSED by name, the
# entrance (before the folds) and the paraboloid (after them) are accepted, both spots = 0.98 f x grad W (f = 10 m).
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_atmos_fold.in
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
old $DECK
none
text
